###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#NonPunitiveWithdrawal
gro-ca:NonPunitiveWithdrawal rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf cco:Role ;
                             rdfs:label "Non-punitive Withdrawal" ;
                             skos:definition "Non-punitive Withdrawal (withdrawal before classes start) is allowed if the student has repaid the total amount funded within 30 days of deposit of funds. If an application cannot be cancelled for the initial disbursement of the application due to issuance of funding through electronic funds transfer, a non-punitive withdrawal will be allowed if the student has repaid the total amount funded within 30 days of deposit of funds. Non-punitive Withdrawal (due to institution closure) If students are withdrawn due to institution closure as outlined in Chapter 9, Section 4, the withdrawal can be considered non-punitive." ;
                             prov:wasDerivedFrom data:CAN_UNIT_00849 .


